===Complete the Era Nova with Phainon{{subst:void|<!--104050109-->}}===
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Unused &mdash; EnterDistrict_G{GroupID})
:'''Lygus:''' But you, Lord Phainon, will bury the old world with that Coreflame, bringing all things into a gray unknown...
::'''Phainon:''' It doesn't matter. This cruel Flame-Chase Journey has made me abandon my fantasies. The future is not a paradise with a gentle west wind, waiting for us to step in...
::'''Phainon:''' If what lies ahead is a mass of chaos, I will tear it apart...
::'''Phainon:''' ...Then usher in the first ray of blazing sunlight.
::'''Phainon:''' ...
::'''Phainon:''' ...Is it you?
::'''Lygus:''' With one last chance to turn back, you still step forward.
::'''Lygus:''' ...How befitting of a Trailblazer.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} This is the path I must take.
:::'''Lygus:''' As it happens, I find myself thinking the exact same thing.
:::Spare me your mockery.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Spare me your mockery.
::'''Lygus:''' (chuckles) You misunderstand.
::'''Lygus:''' As our world nears its end, {{Rubi|the ones who walk the infinite paths|Tribios}} have embraced their destiny...
::'''Lygus:''' As the Theoros, it is my duty to witness the world's future and oversee this final Coreflame ritual on their behalf&mdash;
::'''Lygus:''' The Trial of Worldbearing &mdash; The ritual of Era Nova.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Screwllum says you're behind all this.
::'''Phainon:''' ...?
::'''Lygus:''' Ah, I see. So you met my kindred spirit before I could erase his traces.
::'''Phainon:''' (Trailblazer), what are you saying?
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} This one knows more than he's telling.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Time to make him talk!
::'''Phainon:''' ...
::'''Phainon:''' I've had my suspicions. How does a native Antikytheran know so much about repairing vehicles from beyond the sky?
::'''Phainon:''' Lord Lygus &mdash; How much do you truly know about Era Nova? Tell us everything!
::'''Lygus:''' Hehe...
::'''Lygus:''' Very well, I need no longer maintain this Theoros masquerade. You seek truth, Lord Phainon &mdash; and truth you shall have.
::'''Lygus:''' As you know, when the old gods fell, someone had to bear their broken pillars, to fill the vacant seats. Those who would assume divine authority must prove themselves through trials.
::'''Lygus:''' Yet, for Kephale's demigods, the possibility of overcoming the trials has forever been nonexistent. For the "Worldbearing" trial is the divine duty itself &mdash; bringing forth the "Era Nova" and bearing its weight is an endless ordeal, ceasing only upon collapse.
::'''Lygus:''' Precisely: The "Era Nova" ritual is not something that can be completed in an instant. No, but a long and arduous journey. While the sacrificial journeys of other demigods conclude in this world, Kephale must shoulder the gods' Coreflames, bear the memories of all worlds, and stand unwavering...
::'''Lygus:''' Until the next world... when the black tide consumes the Bearer and all that they carry, leaving nothing behind.
::'''Phainon:''' ...Unless their Coreflame finds a new bearer.
::'''Lygus:''' The holy flame that illuminates all worlds rests in your hands. All that remains is one choice...
::'''Lygus:''' Nurture it, pass it on to future generations, or extinguish it here and now?
::'''Lygus:''' Deliverer, the fate of all worlds rests in your hands.
::'''Phainon:''' Enough testing. I've made my decision.
::'''Phainon:''' But before I ignite the dawn of the next world, you need to promise me something &mdash; two things, actually.
::'''Lygus:''' Speak your terms.
::'''Phainon:''' Promise me this: Professor Anaxa's vision of the "New World" is absolute. The world will be reborn from my memories, all souls, living and dead, will return as the first humans, unchanged from their past lives...
::'''Phainon:''' And my friends &mdash; the fallen demigods, they shall transcend the cycle to become new Titans. Our heroes shall not have died in vain.
::'''Lygus:''' Of course. This I can guarantee.
::'''Phainon:''' Good. The second one&mdash;
::'''Phainon:''' Promise me (Trailblazer) can return safely to {{MC|м=his|ж=her}} homeland, unbound by Amphoreus's laws.
::'''Lygus:''' ...My apologies, but I cannot promise this. As you mentioned, {{MC|ж=she|м=he}} now bears the Time Titan's authority...
::'''Lygus:''' {{MC|м=His|ж=Her}} bonds with this world run too deep.
::'''Phainon:''' ...
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} No need to worry, I have a plan.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Trust me, initiate the Era Nova.
::'''Lygus:''' Well... I stand corrected. An outsider like {{MC|м=him|ж=her}} does have ways to defy destiny.
::{{tx}}
